ok   unwrap(period=8, discont=1.0): steps with |d| > max(discont, period/2) replaced by their period complement (exact)  [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0] vs [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0]
ok   unwrap(period=8, discont=4.0): steps with |d| > max(discont, period/2) replaced by their period complement (exact)  [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0] vs [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0]
ok   unwrap(period=8, discont=5.0): steps with |d| > max(discont, period/2) replaced by their period complement (exact)  [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0] vs [0.0, 3.5, 7.0, 5.0, 9.0, 9.0, 8.0]
FAIL unwrap(period=8, discont=5): a step of exactly 5 = discont is not 'more than max(discont, period/2)' -> kept  [0, -3, -6]
ok   unwrap(discont=4 > pi): a step of 3.5 is left alone
ok   unwrap(default discont = pi): a step of 3.5 becomes 3.5 - 2 pi
ok   unwrap(discont=1 < pi): acts as discont = pi (step 2 kept)
ok   unwrap(2-D, axis=0) == column-wise 1-D unwrap
ok   unwrap default axis=-1 on the transpose
ok   angle(z, deg=True) = degrees(atan2(imag, real)) to 1 ulp, signed zeros follow atan2 (-1-0j -> -180, -0.0 -> 180)
ok   angle(1j, deg=True) == 90.0 and angle(-1, deg=True) == 180.0 exactly
ok   angle of a real array: 0 for positive, pi for negative
ok   clip(a, 5, 2) with a_min > a_max: every value equals a_max (documented)
ok   clip with array bounds broadcasts
ok   clip keeps NaN elements
